pr_body:
- [x] Depends on #10493
- Closes #8390
- Closes #8391

This is a preliminary optimisation of the beatmap carousel. It focuses on reducing the overall memory consumption when scrolling and selecting beatmaps, but does not optimise the beatmap (difficulty) panels.

As such, it not meant to be a final optimisation for this component. It's designed in a way that allows follow-up optimisations to be added locally (beatmap difficulties, panel content alloc avoidance). Things are in state where the memory overhead at song select is reduced by some insane amount, so seems like a good point to PR before it grows any larger.

Benchmark code:

```csharp
    [Test]
    public void TestManyPanels()
    {
        loadBeatmaps(count: 5000, randomDifficulties: true);

        setSelected(1, 1);
        AddWaitStep("wait some", 10);

        setSelected(5000, 1);
        AddWaitStep("wait some", 10);

        AddRepeatStep("scroll much", () => carousel.ScrollContainer.ScrollTo(carousel.ScrollContainer.Current - 1000), 100);

        AddWaitStep("wait some", 10);

        AddStep("collect", GC.Collect);

        AddWaitStep("wait some", 10);

        for (int i = 1; i < 50; i++)
            setSelected(i, 1);

        AddWaitStep("wait some", 10);
    }
```

